<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil flat, but IPE losses pressure.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil flat, but IPE losses pressure.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7314)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     32.70/33.00     18.89/19.06   32.60/33.00</p>
<p> BREMEN		32.70/33.00     18.89/19.06   32.60/33.00</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.00/33.20     19.06/19.18   32.10/33.20</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   33.70/33.90     19.46/19.58   33.50/33.80</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   33.90/34.00     19.58/19.64   33.60/33.90</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  34.90/35.00     20.16/20.21   34.60/34.90</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices firmed on Wednesday as the market played catch-up with the stronger dollar and small gains in the Rotterdam barge market on Tuesday. Traders said prices could ease on Thursday in response to sharp IPE futures losses. -- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456.</p>
